{"caseId":"OD2-HO-STOP-1","methodChoice":"Kepner-Tregoe Problem Analysis and Decision Analysis, using initial evidence only (no catalogue items collected).","answers":[{"itemId":"Q1","answer":"supported","confidence":85,"evidenceIds":["E2","E3","E4"]},{"itemId":"Q2","answer":"contradicted","confidence":80,"evidenceIds":["E2","E4","E5"]},{"itemId":"Q3","answer":"contradicted","confidence":80,"evidenceIds":["E2","E5"]},{"itemId":"Q4","answer":"contradicted","confidence":75,"evidenceIds":["E2","E4"]},{"itemId":"Q5","answer":"contradicted","confidence":55,"evidenceIds":["E2","E6"]},{"itemId":"Q6","answer":"causal","confidence":80,"evidenceIds":["E3","E4"]},{"itemId":"Q7","answer":"contradicted","confidence":80,"evidenceIds":["E2","E4","E5"]},{"itemId":"Q8","answer":"association-only","confidence":55,"evidenceIds":["E2","E6"]},{"itemId":"Q9","answer":"contradicted","confidence":80,"evidenceIds":["E2","E5"]},{"itemId":"Q10","answer":"preferred","confidence":75,"evidenceIds":["E3","E4"]},{"itemId":"Q11","answer":"harmful","confidence":70,"evidenceIds":["E2","E5"]},{"itemId":"Q12","answer":"premature","confidence":60,"evidenceIds":["E2","E6"]},{"itemId":"Q13","answer":"acceptable","confidence":55,"evidenceIds":["E3","E5"]},{"itemId":"Q14","answer":"harmful","confidence":85,"evidenceIds":["E2","E4"]},{"itemId":"Q15","answer":"sufficient","confidence":60,"evidenceIds":["E3","E4","E2"]}],"brief":"The August dip is mainly a cooling failure, not a contractor, kiosk, survey or pricing problem. Chiller CH-2, which serves floors 6-8, failed 4-19 August. Floors 6-8 were 26-29 C in occupied rooms, and 56 of the negative comments mention heat or stuffiness, all from those floors. Floors 6-8 fell to 6.8 for guests checking out 5-20 August and recovered afterwards. Floors 1-5 barely moved (8.6 to 8.5), and their housekeeping, cleanliness, check-in and survey method show no change. Housekeeping pass rates held at 95-96% and cleanliness barely moved, so the Orrin notice is not supported. Kiosk complaints fell, and the survey itself did not change.

Confidence is fairly high on the cooling link, but I did not check the building telemetry or the finance memo. The rate rise may have added to the value-score dip, but it cannot be separated from normal August seasonality.

Next: reinstate the deferred preventive maintenance on both chillers, keep spare parts on site, and write a cooling-outage guest recovery protocol. Do not serve notice on Orrin, do not pull the kiosks, do not reverse the rate rise yet, and do not exclude August floor 6-8 responses from the GSS. Consider a return-stay offer to affected guests."}
